	the tail measure, in the framework of continuous time stochastic
	processes with paths in the space $\mathcal \{D\}$of
	c{\`a}dl{\`a}g functions indexed by $\mathbb \{R\}$, endowed with
	Skorohod's J1 topology. We prove that the essential properties of
	these objects are preserved, with some minor (though interesting)
	differences arising. We first obtain structural results which
	provide representation for homogeneous shift-invariant measures
	on $\mathcal \{D\}$and then study regular variation of random
	elements in $\mathcal \{D\}$. We give practical conditions and
	study several examples, recovering and extending known results.",
	journal  = "Extremes",
